{"summary": "I finished `transpose` in `transpose.py`, and it gives the expected output on the examples I tried.

It pads each row with spaces up to the length of the longest row below it, then reads off the columns. That way short rows put spaces on the left of the output, and no extra spaces get added on the right. Spaces that were already in the input stay in the output.

I checked it by hand on `ABC\nDE` → `AD\nBE\nC`, `AB\nDEF` → `AD\nBE\n F`, the "TEASER" triangle, and empty input. The project has no test files, so these spot checks are the only verification."}
